# Test: a command that declares only a summary publishes no long explanation
# VALIDATES: AC-6, the zero-value half -- ze help command --json carries
#            `description` and NO `long-help` key for a command whose YANG node
#            declares a description and no ze:help
# PREVENTS: a reader inventing a long form out of the summary, which is what
#           every deleted guess did
# NOTE: this file runs ONE command on purpose. A reject=stdout matches the
#       ACCUMULATED stdout of every command in the file, so a second command
#       here would leave the negative assertion meaningless
#       (docs/architecture/testing/ci-format.md). `veth` selects exactly one
#       catalog entry, and internal/component/iface/yang/ze-iface-cmd.yang
#       declares it with a description and no ze:help.

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze help command veth --json
expect=exit:code=0

expect=stdout:contains="path": "create interface veth name"
expect=stdout:contains="description": "Create a veth pair (two linked virtual Ethernet interfaces)."

# Nothing invents a long form. The key is absent, not empty.
reject=stdout:contains="long-help"
